{"type": "batch_patient_confound", "columns": ["batch", "patient"], "confirmed": true, "evidence": "Cramer's V = 1.0 with a perfect one-to-one mapping (B1=P4, B2=P1, B3=P5, B4=P3, B5=P6, B6=P2). Per-batch sex-gene fractions are identical to the per-patient ones, so batches do not mix patients as the design requires."},
{"type": "sample_swap", "columns": ["sample", "patient", "sex"], "confirmed": true, "evidence": "Patient P2 (recorded M) is 18.6% XIST+ and 61.3% RPS4Y1+; patient P3 (recorded F) is 69.3% XIST+ and 17.4% RPS4Y1+. Other patients of the same sex show about 2% or 84% for these genes. The mixed signal sits in P2_pre (37% XIST+, 43% RPS4Y1+) and P3_pre (35% RPS4Y1+, 50% XIST+), while P2_post and P3_post look clean. This is consistent with cells swapped between P2_pre and P3_pre."}
]}
```

